WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.315
I decided to develop a camera

00:00:03.315 --> 00:00:08.395
with an exposure time of 100 years.

00:00:08.395 --> 00:00:13.855
Now the camera is not your ordinary device

00:00:13.855 --> 00:00:17.115
it's not your iPhone for instance. It is

00:00:17.115 --> 00:00:20.075
in fact the simplest of cameras because

00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:22.075
anything complicated is liable to break.

00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:23.924
And I probably couldn't make it anyway.

00:00:23.924 --> 00:00:27.645
So what I have done, starting in Berlin,

00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:30.575
was to make a camera that is a pinhole camera.

00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:33.275
In other words it's a camera that

00:00:33.284 --> 00:00:35.325
lets in very little light through a

00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:38.085
pinhole that is focused onto what

00:00:38.085 --> 00:00:42.315
ordinarily would be a piece of film.

00:00:42.315 --> 00:00:45.194
Well any film is going to spoil relatively

00:00:45.194 --> 00:00:47.025
quickly. I've managed to with my own

00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:49.755
cyanotype chemistry make exposures that

00:00:49.755 --> 00:00:53.775
are on the order of perhaps a week. And

00:00:53.775 --> 00:00:55.635
I know people who have managed to do so

00:00:55.635 --> 00:00:58.574
I believe up to a couple years through

00:00:58.575 --> 00:01:01.655
various tricks. And that's well and good.

00:01:01.655 --> 00:01:03.375
But it certainly is by no means

00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:05.925
a century. So the way in which this camera

00:01:05.925 --> 00:01:09.375
works is it doesn't use ordinary film.

00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:10.934
It uses something much more common and

00:01:10.935 --> 00:01:12.615
much more simple which is ordinary

00:01:12.615 --> 00:01:15.195
black paper. Now if you think about a book

00:01:15.195 --> 00:01:17.355
on your coffee table, for instance, and you

00:01:17.355 --> 00:01:20.535
look at it... you'll see that it

00:01:20.535 --> 00:01:22.785
probably has started to fade or a poster

00:01:22.785 --> 00:01:24.675
on your wall. And it will continue to do so

00:01:24.675 --> 00:01:28.125
in sunlight well the same thing will

00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:31.665
happen for a piece of ordinary black paper.

00:01:31.665 --> 00:01:33.845
But if you put that paper into a camera

00:01:33.845 --> 00:01:36.254
letting in very little light through

00:01:36.254 --> 00:01:37.905
a pinhole, what you're doing is you're

00:01:37.905 --> 00:01:40.394
projecting the scene in front of the

00:01:40.394 --> 00:01:43.875
camera. But light is projected on to the

00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:46.305
paper in a way that the paper will

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:49.995
gradually bleach, very very slowly taking

00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:53.114
in an image. The image will not be static

00:01:53.115 --> 00:01:55.815
because presumably whatever you're

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.335
photographing is going to change over

00:01:58.335 --> 00:01:59.864
that 100-year period. So if you think

00:01:59.864 --> 00:02:02.415
about if the camera is out in a city

00:02:02.415 --> 00:02:04.844
and there are some small houses. And those

00:02:04.844 --> 00:02:07.695
houses get torn down after 20 years and a

00:02:07.695 --> 00:02:09.465
skyscraper gets built up in their place

00:02:09.465 --> 00:02:11.955
and is there for the next 80,

00:02:11.955 --> 00:02:14.475
just to simplify. You would see

00:02:14.475 --> 00:02:18.225
the shadow, a ghost of those houses, against

00:02:18.225 --> 00:02:20.234
the bolder skyscraper sort of like

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.124
in sports photography when you see a

00:02:22.124 --> 00:02:23.915
basketball player moving very fast

00:02:23.915 --> 00:02:26.715
across a court where the court is very

00:02:26.715 --> 00:02:29.954
boldly in place in view and the

00:02:29.954 --> 00:02:31.695
basketball player is sort of ghostly. And

00:02:31.695 --> 00:02:34.245
so what you end up with is not so much

00:02:34.245 --> 00:02:36.465
a photograph as you end up with a movie

00:02:36.465 --> 00:02:39.585
all in a single frame of that full span

00:02:39.585 --> 00:02:43.235
of a hundred years. Now why that

00:02:43.235 --> 00:02:47.195
interested me in Berlin was watching

00:02:47.195 --> 00:02:50.954
the city undergoing rapid and rampant

00:02:50.954 --> 00:02:53.895
development--so incredibly fast that

00:02:53.895 --> 00:02:55.575
every time that I went back there it was as if

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.915
it were a different city. And so I

00:02:57.915 --> 00:03:00.435
started to think about how you might

00:03:00.435 --> 00:03:03.195
make a camera that would be able to

00:03:03.195 --> 00:03:07.055
take that in. That would serve as a sort of a

00:03:07.055 --> 00:03:10.124
surveillance camera in the hands

00:03:10.124 --> 00:03:13.755
of those most affected by everything that

00:03:13.755 --> 00:03:15.285
we do, all the decisions that we make, yet

00:03:15.285 --> 00:03:17.985
least powerful to make any decisions:

00:03:17.985 --> 00:03:20.325
that is to say those not yet born. And so

00:03:20.325 --> 00:03:23.025
the idea in Berlin was to build these

00:03:23.025 --> 00:03:26.115
cameras as surveillance cameras that

00:03:26.115 --> 00:03:28.065
could be taken out into the field

00:03:28.065 --> 00:03:31.244
and hidden away and in a hundred years

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.675
the images would be brought in. So

00:03:33.675 --> 00:03:37.274
I worked with a gallery called "team titanic"

00:03:37.274 --> 00:03:40.994
we built a hundred of them. And we then made

00:03:40.994 --> 00:03:42.885
them available to anyone who wanted

00:03:42.885 --> 00:03:45.045
to take one and to hide it. If you wanted to

00:03:45.045 --> 00:03:48.255
take one you gave a deposit of 10 euros,

00:03:48.255 --> 00:03:50.395
took a camera, hid it somewhere.

00:03:50.395 --> 00:03:52.415
Anywhere that you wanted in Berlin didn't tell

00:03:52.425 --> 00:03:54.195
anybody. Except when you got to be

00:03:54.195 --> 00:03:56.985
very old you would tell a child where you had

00:03:56.985 --> 00:03:59.975
put it. Or you would write it into your will.

00:03:59.975 --> 00:04:02.654
And in a hundred years

00:04:02.654 --> 00:04:06.075
those children then grown up would bring

00:04:06.075 --> 00:04:09.915
the cameras back to team titanic where

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.374
they would get the 10 euro deposit.

00:04:12.375 --> 00:04:14.615
No guarantees about what it's worth.

00:04:14.615 --> 00:04:16.995
But nevertheless you would get something

00:04:16.995 --> 00:04:18.075
in return and then there would be

00:04:18.075 --> 00:04:21.555
an exhibition. A hundred years of change, all

00:04:21.555 --> 00:04:24.465
in that image. And so the idea was really

00:04:24.465 --> 00:04:27.735
to engage people. To engage the children of

00:04:27.735 --> 00:04:30.945
today in a way that they were actively

00:04:30.945 --> 00:04:34.275
taking a part in putting these cameras

00:04:34.275 --> 00:04:36.825
out in the world. And not only those who

00:04:36.825 --> 00:04:39.795
were directly involved, but also those

00:04:39.795 --> 00:04:42.345
who heard about it, who read about it.

00:04:42.345 --> 00:04:45.105
And it was all over the place we got it into

00:04:45.105 --> 00:04:47.775
the newspapers. We got a conversation

00:04:47.775 --> 00:04:50.895
going about this. That the cameras

00:04:50.895 --> 00:04:54.975
became a sort of a constant presence

00:04:54.975 --> 00:04:56.855
and remain for the next 100 years a sort of

00:04:56.865 --> 00:04:58.845
constant presence in the city. Think of them as

00:04:58.845 --> 00:05:01.215
sort of black boxes in that sense.

00:05:01.215 --> 00:05:06.075
That are documenting and therefore are, well,

00:05:06.075 --> 00:05:08.235
it's a sort of documentary photography

00:05:08.235 --> 00:05:09.875
in the worst possible way.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.915
Because documentary photographers are not

00:05:11.925 --> 00:05:14.405
supposed to interfere. These photographs

00:05:14.405 --> 00:05:17.595
manifestly do interfere because

00:05:17.595 --> 00:05:20.205
you don't know where they are and yet you

00:05:20.205 --> 00:05:23.145
know that you could be being watched.

00:05:23.145 --> 00:05:25.695
And so the decisions that you make

00:05:25.695 --> 00:05:27.015
you perhaps feel a little bit more

00:05:27.015 --> 00:05:29.655
accountable for those and perhaps feel

00:05:29.655 --> 00:05:32.775
some sort of a relationship to those

00:05:32.775 --> 00:05:33.935
in the far future.

